Intro: 
Instagram launched in October 2010 and immediately gained traction, amassing about 25,000 users on its first day. It's focus on mobile photo ahring and it suite of image-enhancing filters quickly brought users on board. 

By April 2012, Instagram was acquired by Facebook, now Meta Platforms, Inc. (META), for 1 billion.

2013 to 2016: Expansion 
Introduction of Direct Messages, marking entry into private communication. They launched Stories. Instagram Shopping debuts, transforming the platform into an e-commerce destination. 





Instagram makes money through advertising, eCommerce integration, brand partnership, and sponsored content. 


